From 2d83bb8a511c3c08d91a2fe6c52ac431d8e40f87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pypto-x-agent <agent@pypto-x.local>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 02:35:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 257/258] fix(execution): reconcile report copies against the
 embedded plan payload

Close the verify-0044 claim-5 missing class: the report could rewrite its own
copies of plan-level facts while leaving plan_payload.document (the
resolution.plan_digest preimage) untouched, producing a document that
contradicted its own embedded plan.

* report copies of plan facts are now byte-compared with the embedded
  payload: request (op/shapes/dtype/policy_digest), requested_policy,
  resolved_policy (incl. fallback.chain/primary/used/degraded),
  policy_applicability, layout_decision (modulo the runtime alias_check),
  resolution.{candidates,rejections,rules,numeric_class_order,tie_break,
  fallback_chain,fallback_primary}, dispatch.provider_declared, the target /
  capability / contract views, and (without a runtime fallback) the
  probe-variable resolved.library/artifact.library;
* named refusals: report_numeric_class_order_not_reconciled,
  report_tie_break_not_reconciled, report_fallback_chain_not_reconciled,
  report_fallback_primary_not_reconciled,
  report_fallback_degraded_not_reconciled,
  report_plan_payload_copy_not_reconciled (plus the existing library reason
  for probe fields);
* the fully coordinated alternate payload remains the registered residual
  and is now the only way to move request/policy/trace/fallback facts;
* hermetic focused test fix: the R4 coherent-rewrite regression re-derives
  the plan-level thread mode from the rewritten counts + requested policy and
  syncs the payload/decision/report runtime modes, so it no longer depends on
  the process-global BLIS thread state left by earlier api_pinned runs;
  canonical order 336 passed x2 (was 1 failed/328 passed);
* tests: 5 parametrized report-copy cases for the missing class, the request
  block and the probe library field; all genuine reports (10) still pass;
* docs: 0006 section 3.2/7.1 and the brief classify every payload-backed
  report copy as reconciled and the alternate-payload/no-attestation classes
  as residuals.
